  "comments": {
    "@n8cjrp10l4dib602jd6ipajkin": "a + b, part by part: for points, directions, colours, or any record whose fields are all Numbers. This module's operations and their names follow the built-in functions of GLSL and WGSL (influence), which a shader compiles them to.",
    "@kvbhh6cksqp17efkalda17cpt2": "a − b, part by part. The direction from b to a.",
    "@3t201ikphr7rllhpfin325re2k": "a · b, part by part: a colour tinted by another.",
    "@gpr2icg8543tmnss26ricahd08": "Every part of v times by: a direction made longer, a colour made brighter.",
    "@bsh2hsvcrpov7nqglt3ehur72p": "The parts' products added up: how much a and b point the same way.",
    "@bao90prcj22ricdcuiurqbqm3e": "How long v is: √(v · v).",
    "@muecrc8oiijgl4bombeo3iqn9o": "How far a is from b.",
    "@qiqooshfclqatv3j6af0khn4fu": "v scaled to length 1 (normalize on a GPU).",
    "@vshgss85bifvhke0t02estkjid": "a when amount is 0, b when it is 1, and in between, part by part.",
    "@m391m4mr8rc457pi2icf8foqik": "Every part of v kept between low and high.",
    "@ssv7tptarl9u1ahrb3h5uhakms": "A ray going this direction, bounced off a surface facing normal (normal of length 1)."
  },
